# W2-AR-05 -- a data file missing in the middle of a session must not kill
# the process. Run with RA2_INSTALL_DIR pointing at an install copy WITHOUT
# Maps01.mix (the Allied campaign maps): starting the Allied campaign shows
# the error page naming the file, and MAIN MENU returns to the shell.
#   $env:RA2_INSTALL_DIR = "<install copy without Maps01.mix>\"
# R-183: on a FULL install (no optional file missing) the scenario cannot be
# reproduced, so the script logs SKIPPED and passes without checking.
set render_every 300
set on_quit continue

if data_missing_optional == 0 then log SKIPPED: full install (point RA2_INSTALL_DIR at a copy without Maps01.mix)
if data_missing_optional == 0 then end
click button "Single Player"
click button "New Campaign"
require scene == "shell:Campaign"
click well:allied
click button Load
until 30 scene == campaign-load
click start
until 300 scene == error
require scene == error
shot error
click button "MAIN MENU"
until 60 scene == "shell:Main Menu"
require scene == "shell:Main Menu"
end
